net: ipv6: ip6mr: Fix in/out netdev to pass to the FORWARD chain

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.4.1.el9_9
commit-author Petr Machata <petrm@nvidia.com>
commit 3365afd3abda5f6a54f4a822dad5c9314e94c3fc
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.4.1.el9_9/3365afd3.failed

The netfilter hook is invoked with skb->dev for input netdevice, and
vif_dev for output netdevice. However at the point of invocation, skb->dev
is already set to vif_dev, and MR-forwarded packets are reported with
in=out:

 # ip6tables -A FORWARD -j LOG --log-prefix '[forw]'
 # cd tools/testing/selftests/net/forwarding
 # ./router_multicast.sh
 # dmesg | fgrep '[forw]'
 [ 1670.248245] [forw]IN=v5 OUT=v5 [...]

For reference, IPv4 MR code shows in and out as appropriate.
Fix by caching skb->dev and using the updated value for output netdev.

Fixes: 7bc570c8b4f7 ("[IPV6] MROUTE: Support multicast forwarding.")
	Signed-off-by: Petr Machata <petrm@nvidia.com>
	Reviewed-by: Ido Schimmel <idosch@nvidia.com>
	Reviewed-by: Nikolay Aleksandrov <razor@blackwall.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/3141ae8386fbe13fef4b793faa75e6bae58d798a.1750113335.git.petrm@nvidia.com
	Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 3365afd3abda5f6a54f4a822dad5c9314e94c3fc)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
diff --cc net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
index 2a4511768e42,426859cd3409..000000000000
--- a/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
@@@ -2006,9 -2038,10 +2006,15 @@@ static inline int ip6mr_forward2_finish
  static int ip6mr_forward2(struct net *net, struct mr_table *mrt,
  			  struct sk_buff *skb, int vifi)
  {
++<<<<<<< HEAD
++=======
+ 	struct vif_device *vif = &mrt->vif_table[vifi];
+ 	struct net_device *indev = skb->dev;
+ 	struct net_device *vif_dev;
++>>>>>>> 3365afd3abda (net: ipv6: ip6mr: Fix in/out netdev to pass to the FORWARD chain)
  	struct ipv6hdr *ipv6h;
 +	struct vif_device *vif = &mrt->vif_table[vifi];
 +	struct net_device *dev;
  	struct dst_entry *dst;
  	struct flowi6 fl6;
  
@@@ -2069,7 -2102,7 +2075,11 @@@
  	IP6CB(skb)->flags |= IP6SKB_FORWARDED;
  
  	return NF_HOOK(NFPROTO_IPV6, NF_INET_FORWARD,
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		       net, NULL, skb, skb->dev, dev,
++=======
+ 		       net, NULL, skb, indev, skb->dev,
++>>>>>>> 3365afd3abda (net: ipv6: ip6mr: Fix in/out netdev to pass to the FORWARD chain)
  		       ip6mr_forward2_finish);
  
  out_free:
* Unmerged path net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
